# SDEMO-T03: Demo Seed Data

## Objective

Add a `seed:demo` script that populates work-control with a realistic demo state:
one chat thread, one accepted epic, a board with 3 tasks (DONE / IN_PROGRESS / TODO).
Audience sees a non-empty UI immediately — no need to type to get started.

## App-agent preflight

- [ ] MCP preflight §2
- [ ] `explain("work-control")` — confirm repo interface (chat, epic, board, tasks)
- [ ] Read `apps/work-control/server/repo/types.ts` — WorkControlRepo interface

## Implementation

### 1. Create seed script

File: `apps/work-control/scripts/seed-demo.ts`

```ts
// SEE: feature "work-control" at core/docs/knowledge/work-control.md
import { createWorkControlRepo } from '../server/repo'

const repo = createWorkControlRepo()

async function seed() {
  // 1 chat
  const chat = await repo.createChat({ title: 'App Agent Demo' })

  // 1 epic (accepted)
  const epic = await repo.createEpic({
    chatId: chat.id,
    title: 'Build a public demo of App Agent',
    description: 'Showcase the chat → epic → board → task execution loop.',
    targetApp: 'work-control',
    status: 'ACCEPTED'
  })

  // 1 sprint plan
  const sprint = await repo.createSprint({
    epicId: epic.id,
    title: 'S01 - Demo Sprint',
    gate: 'OPEN'
  })

  // 3 tasks
  await repo.createTask({ sprintId: sprint.id, title: 'Design the demo flow', status: 'DONE', leadRole: 'ARCHITECT' })
  await repo.createTask({ sprintId: sprint.id, title: 'Build the deploy pipeline', status: 'IN_PROGRESS', leadRole: 'DEVOPS' })
  await repo.createTask({ sprintId: sprint.id, title: 'Write the product page', status: 'TODO', leadRole: 'PM' })

  console.log('Demo seed complete')
}

seed().catch(console.error)
```

> Adjust method names to match actual `WorkControlRepo` interface — read `types.ts` first.

### 2. Add to package.json scripts

In `apps/work-control/package.json`:
```json
"seed:demo": "bun run scripts/seed-demo.ts"
```

### 3. Run locally to verify

```bash
cd /Users/denistka/Projects/app-agent-io/DAWWWB-app-agent
bun run --filter=@app-agent/work-control seed:demo
```

Then open `http://localhost:3003` — board should show the 3 seeded tasks.

### 4. Railway: run seed post-deploy

Option A (simplest): run manually via Railway CLI once after deploy:
```bash
railway run bun apps/work-control/scripts/seed-demo.ts
```

Option B: add to `startCommand` with a seed check (skip if data exists).

## Done when

- [ ] `seed:demo` script runs without error
- [ ] Board page shows 3 seeded tasks in correct columns
- [ ] Chat shows the demo chat in sidebar
- [ ] Script is idempotent (safe to run twice — check-before-insert)
